   derivative p is the velocity, and \{m(j)\} are the principal masses
   m(j)(-1) = partial derivative(epsilon,n)(2)/partial derivative p(j)(2)
   along the normal and the two principal axes of curvatures at each point
   of the constant-energy surface represented by epsilon = epsilon(n)(p).
