   SCI RES; RHONE ALPES REG; CITY GRENOBLE},
Abstract = {The substitution of a small fraction of Cu atoms by Fe atoms in the
   cooper oxide superconductors has proven to be useful in sensing, with
   Mossbauer spectroscopy, the local surroundings of the Cu sites of their
   structures. In this work we report the results of such substitution in
   the Nd1.85Ce0.15Cu2O4-delta system. After annealing in argon at high
   pressure and temperature, a strong quadrupole doublet is observed
   indicating that the iron atoms have been incorporated into the
   superconductor structure.},
