Year = {1993},
Volume = {54},
Number = {1},
Pages = {23-28},
Abstract = {Developing seeds of Ipomoea purpurea were analysed for proteins from
   anthesis to maturity. The total amount was highest at maturity; albumins
   were predominant, followed by globulins and prolamins. At the begining,
   the proteins occur in the seed covers. Later they appear in large amouns
   in the embryo, especially around the procambium, the epicotyl and very
   conspicuously in the cotyledons. At naturity, intense staining occurs in
   the testa and in the embryo, particularly in the cotyledons.},
