Year = {1991},
Volume = {19},
Number = {2},
Pages = {88-92},
Abstract = {Eremochelis lagunensis new species from Palo Extrano in Baja California
   Sur, Mexico, is described and illustrated.  The structure of the fixed
   finger of the male chelicerae of E. lagunensis looks like the fixed
   fingers of E. rossi Muma, 1986 but the fondal notch and mesoventral
   groove of the fixed finger as well as the dentition of the movable
   finger of E. lagunensis are different from that species.  The females
   are similar to E. truncus.},
