Abstract = {A collection C of subsets of a set X is said to be Noetherian if C does
   not contain a strictly increasing infinite chain.  A space X is
   Noetherianly refinable, or more briefly, N - refinable, if each open
   covering of X has a Noetherian open refinement which covers X.  A base B
   for a topological space X is an ortho - base if for each B'
   subset-or-equal-to B, either intersectB' is an open set of X or
   intersectB' = \{p\} and B' is a local base at p.  We show that every T1
   - space with an ortho-base has a Noetherian base if and only if each of
   its open subspaces is N - refinable.},
